VF(1)                          ZOAU Command Syntax                         VF(1)

NAME

	vf - Print information about active Direct Access Storage Devices.

SYNOPSIS

	vf [-dhjJUv] [VOLSER]

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-j
		Print output in JSON format.

	-J
		Prints formatted JSON output.
		This option forces -j if it was not set.

	-U
		Print available and total space in 'human-readable' format, such as
		1.1K, 42M, or 123G, where 1K = 1024 bytes.

	-v
		Print out verbose information.

DESCRIPTION

	List space and status information for all active DASD volumes,
	or a single volume serial if VOLSER is specified.
	Free and total space is calculated using the constants for a 3390 device.

	Output has the following fields:
		<unit> <volser> <available> <total> <percentage used> <status> <flags> <free tracks> <total tracks>

	<unit>
		Four character device number.

	<volser>
		Serial number of the volume.

	<available>
		Available volume space, in kilobytes. 

	<total>
		Total volume space, in kilobytes. 

	<percentage used>
		Volume space in use, as a percentage.

	<status>
		Hexadecimal representation of the status bytes that correspond to
		"UCBSTAT" in the Unit Control Block (UCB).
		Device status flags:
		 - UCBONLI (0x80) Device is online.
		 - UCBCHGS (0x40) Device status is set to change from online to offline,
		   and either allocation is enqueued on devices or the device is 
		   allocated. (Bit UCBONLI is also on.)
		 - UCBRESV (0x20) The mount status of the volume on this device
		   is reserved.
		 - UCBUNLD (0x10) Unload operator command has been addressed to
		   this device. The device is not unloaded yet.
		 - UCBALOC (0x08) Device is allocated. For auto-switchable devices,
		   this bit indicates that the device was allocated by some system
		   in the SYSPLEX at the time that allocation last obtained the
		   SYSPLEX allocation status.
		 - UCBPRES (0x04) The volume is permanently resident on this device.
		 - UCBSYSR (0x02) System residence device, primary console, or
		   active console.
		 - UCBDADI (0x01) Standard tape labels have been verified for this
		   tape volume or secondary console or console status changing.
	
	<flags>
		Additional information flags in this order:
		 - "t" or "c": Indicates the volume space information shows track or cylinder managed space.
		 - "e": Index exists for VTOC, "-" otherwise.
		 - "a": Index VTOC active, "-" otherwise.

	<free tracks>
		Number of free tracks.

	<total tracks>
		Number of total tracks.

	JSON output has this structure:
		{ 
		"data": {
			"volumes": [
				{
					"unit": <string>,
					"volser": <string>,
					"status": {
						"UCBONLI": <boolean>,
						"UCBCHGS": <boolean>,
						"UCBRESV": <boolean>,
						"UCBUNLD": <boolean>,
						"UCBALOC": <boolean>,
						"UCBPRES": <boolean>,
						"UCBSYSR": <boolean>,
						"UCBDADI": <boolean>
					},
					"is_cylinder_managed": <boolean>,
					"index_vtoc": <boolean>,
					"vtoc_active": <boolean>,
					"free_space": <string>,
					"total_space": <string>,
					"free_kilobytes": <number>,
					"total_kilobytes": <number>,
					"percentage_used": <number>,
					"free_tracks": <number>,
					"total_tracks": <number>,
				},
				{ ... }
			],
			"errors": [
				{
					"unit": <string>,
					"volser": <string>,
					"status": { ... },
					"LSPACE_message": <string>
				},
				{ ... }
			],
			},
		"volumes_reported": <number>,
		"errors_encountered": <number>
		}

EXAMPLES

	Display all available information for active volumes, with formatted space values:

		vf -U

	Display information only for volume serial 'VOL123':

		vf VOL123

	Print a JSON string with information for all volumes:

		vf -j

	List and sort all volumes by space used, in descending order:

		vf | sort -k 5 -r

EXIT VALUES

	0
		vf completed successfully.

	2
		Syntax error. Correct the vf syntax and resubmit the command.

	4
		Bad option or argument specified.

	8
		Error occurred. See error messages for details.
